{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1517308-building-a-monster-slasher-for-my-group","id":1517308,"title":"Building a monster/slasher for my group","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-06T13:34:31-07:00","id":1517308,"title":"Building a monster/slasher for my group","content":"I'm a ST for a group. We're playing 1e as I don't have 2e books. <br /> <br /> One of my player's backstory in why she became a Hunter is that she lost her husband after confronting the priest at a parish and accused him of multiple things having to do with the youth at the church. Basically he came after her one evening thinking she was alone and her cop husband died trying to protect her <br /> <br /> I'm debating if I should just make a slasher that's a bullet sponge, but we also discussed that it could be some kind of face stealing monster thing. I'm not making it a vampire because it could function during the daytime. <br /> <br /> My idea was that maybe it's some kind of entity that infiltrates families or a community as some kind of dark father/step-father then consumes like the children's youth/life or something. <br /> <br /> Right now they're hunting a different monster as I haven't fleshed out this guy as part of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27979-lati-knight","name":"Lati-knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T14:25:51-07:00","id":1517310,"title":"","content":"A Changeling might do. Feeds on terror and other emotions, which would make good fodder for the original accusations. Their Contracts make for a good excuse for unnatural survivability too, and they have the built-in weakness of Iron to exploit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T04:25:37-07:00","id":1517342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1517308-building-a-monster-slasher-for-my-group?p=1517310#post1517310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Changeling might do. Feeds on terror and other emotions, which would make good fodder for the original accusations. Their Contracts make for a good excuse for unnatural survivability too, and they have the built-in weakness of Iron to exploit</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna second that. A Changeling might make for a supernatural threat that is both classic and out of the left field for most players.","signature":"","edited":{"